        internal static BehaviourCatalog.FactDefinition Live()=>new("object.container.live",OutputType(Object(new JObject{
            ["sessionId"]=Text("^[a-f0-9]{32}$",32),["phase"]=Choice("idle","waiting","flowing","failed"),["contents"]=Object(new JObject{["amountMl"]=Number(0,32000000),["savedAmountMl"]=Number(0,32000000),["capacityMl"]=Number(1,32000000),["transferredMl"]=Number(0,256000000),["spilledMl"]=Number(0,256000000)}),["temporary"]=new JObject{["type"]="boolean"},["error"]=Text("^.{0,128}$",128)})),"Live container contents","Current native liquid quantity during physical pouring or scooping, separate from the last accepted object.container definition. Flowing contents are published together after 0.3 seconds without flow, at grip release, pause or Save, at bounded ten-second checkpoints, and before an empty participating vessel adopts a different liquid identity or colour; one Undo restores that episode. Acceptance updates live contents immediately; persistence runs in order off the interaction thread with at most two queued checkpoints. Full storage admission pauses additional intake, never accrues skipped time, and does not freeze vessel movement. A failed save keeps accepted quantities as unconfirmed and blocks further saves until explicit workspace recovery. Read world.liquidPersistence for durability; savedAmountMl is the last journal-accepted amount, not proof of disk persistence. transferredMl/spilledMl are outgoing pouring totals for this source in the current episode, reset at journal acceptance. Scooping has separate object.container.scooping counters. No per-drop rigidbodies, carried fluid mass or mixing. Terrain reservoirs share the same measured inventory, level and publication. Shared bounded buoyancy/drag is described by object.medium. Amounts use logical millilitres independent of visual resizing. Waiting means complete transfer-work capacity or this container interaction group's required spatial inputs are unavailable; error explains it. Before changing quantities, each complete interacting group prepares relevant saved solids, ground and receiving/donor cavities, including empty or offset cavities and rain cover. Quantity paths close transitively, including retained or anchored dormant poses and connected moving bodies; sharing a read-only obstacle or roof alone does not join separate groups. Ready independent groups can advance while another waits or loads. Each complete quantity group receives its own execution allowance, atomically coupled with its moving-body dependencies. Independent groups do not pay for unrelated dormant inventory. Preparation includes streams that a currently empty tilted receiver could produce after earlier intake in that same pass, and rain cover for cavities that could drain before collection. Missing geometry is never treated as an empty path. Regrouping already-ready inputs preserves the live episode. If a group that owns unfinished quantities needs unavailable inputs, the existing shared episode publishes before preparation and releases its writer before callbacks. Continued waiting does not repeatedly checkpoint independent flow. All groups still share atomic journal acceptance; skipped time is not accrued. Passive facts never load geometry or restart physics. Inspect runtime.flowWorkBudget and runtime.flowWorkReservation.",Object(new JObject{["target"]=DrawingData.Target()}),new JObject{["target"]=new string('0',32)},(c,a)=>{var data=c.Editor?c.Editor.Liquids?.Observe((string)a["target"]):null;return data==null?null:ProgramValue.Literal(data);},features:new[]{Feature});
        internal static BehaviourCatalog.FactDefinition Persistence()=>new("world.liquidPersistence",OutputType(Object(new JObject{
