            Object(new JObject()),new JObject(),(c,a)=>c.Editor?ProgramValue.Literal(c.Editor.ObserveLiquidPersistence()):null,features:new[]{Feature});
        internal static BehaviourCatalog.EventDefinition Poured()=>new("object.container.poured","A physical pour was saved","A native pouring episode was accepted by the shared room journal (or temporary fork). Value/source is the outgoing vessel ID. transferredMl is the total received by containers; spilledMl left the bounded container model, and does not imply a persistent puddle. receivers counts distinct receiving containers. Emitted in acceptance order at a safe episode boundary after successful publication only; failed saves, cancellation, Undo and reload do not emit/replay it. Continuous flow checkpoints after ten seconds. Before an empty participating vessel changes liquid identity or colour, the prior episode publishes first; new intake is reconsidered next tick. Each outgoing total therefore retains its own liquid identity. Each checkpoint releases its own write lease before callbacks; later queued checkpoints may still own writers. If a listener changes the accepted room or begins another episode, remaining events from the old source are discarded. An intervening authored change or Undo affecting a participant, a changed workspace or replaced native participant discards its stale notification. Moving the whole world while saving does not revoke a valid quantity event. Paused lifecycle listeners may miss the event; inspect current contents instead.",Object(new JObject{["transferredMl"]=Number(0,256000000),["spilledMl"]=Number(0,256000000),["receivers"]=Number(0,16,true),["liquid"]=Text("^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_]{0,31}$",32),["temporary"]=new JObject{["type"]="boolean"}}),objectEvent:true,features:new[]{Feature});
